# Planted "fixes" to the recorded write skew. Each one must make the
# declared anomaly stop reproducing, which flips the outcome and fails
# the check that expects it.
run fv-elle History.edn
properties G2-item G1c-realtime
file History.edn

mutation process 1 waits for process 0's already-committed append
detects G2-item
- {:index 3, :type :ok,     :process 1, :value [[:append 2 20] [:r 1 []]]}
+ {:index 3, :type :ok,     :process 1, :value [[:append 2 20] [:r 1 [10]]]}

mutation process 0 claims to see process 1's append before process 1 made it
detects G1c-realtime
- {:index 1, :type :ok,     :process 0, :value [[:append 1 10] [:r 2 []]]}
+ {:index 1, :type :ok,     :process 0, :value [[:append 1 10] [:r 2 [20]]]}

harmless extra whitespace in the first operation
- {:index 0, :type :invoke, :process 0, :value [[:append 1 10] [:r 2 nil]]}
+ {:index 0, :type :invoke, :process 0, :value [[:append 1 10] [:r 2 nil]] }
